Julian Corallo <jcorallo@gw.ford.com> writes:
> At present the RZ23's are each mounted on 4 screws/rubber-grommets,
> which slot into the computer chassis.
>
> So do all (non-dec) scsi disks have the same screw holes in the same
> place? Or am I going to have to invent a mounting bracket for non-dec
> disks?

  Almost all disks have the same mounting holes. The only ones I know of
that are different still have the bottom 4 holes that you need in the
same place.

  The oddball rubber feet that DEC uses are non-standard, however. A trick
you can use is to go to Radio Shack and buy their bag of assorted grommets.
One of the smaller grommet sizes fits in the DEC slots just fine. You'll
also need 6-32 screws, either 1/4" or 3/8" long, and flat metal washers
(to keep the screw heads from pulling through the grommets).

  This isn't quite as robust as the DEC feet, so if you're going to ship
the system after mounting the drives, I'd suggest dismounting the drives
and packing/shipping them separately.

