Tom Grossi wrote:
> 
> I have a powerstorm 4D50T graphics card in my Digital Personal
> workstation and I am trying to
> figure out how to change the screen resoultion (and possibly bit
> depth).  How can I do this?  Thanks in advance.  -Tom

Add options of the following form to /var/X11/Xserver.conf at an
appropriate position before any '-I' option:

   -screen[<scr_num>] <width>[x<height>] -vsync[<scr_num>] <vert_rate>

Where:

	<scr_num>	Is an optional screen number (defaults to 0)
	<width>		Desired horizontal res
	<height>	Desired vertical res
	<vert_rate>	Desired vertical refresh rate in Hz.

For the 4D40T-4D60T cards, additional information is in the Open3D
release notes and, in recent kits, in 'man ingr'.

Also for these cards, a large set of visual types is always available.
Forcing the display down to 8bpp or 16bpp won't increase available
resolution.  Dropping resolution, however, may allow other
capabilities such as OpenGL quad buffering.

