an earlier thread on the subject.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
There are a number of ways to get around this.

1).  (smile) use a scsi ribbon cable and remove the wires past #44.
      remove the end of the cable with a file, until it fits in the
      'onboard' IDE connector.

2).  part #FC530 (2" miniIDE44 to miniIDE44 cable) $10 & shipping $5
     HardData Ltd, 11060 - 166 Avenue, Edmonton, AB, Canada - T5X1Y3
     (403) 456-1510  email: harddata@bigfoot.com


The Multia does not have 'much juice', so it is either the internal
scsi or internal ide AND NOT BOTH --- also, you will take a perform-
ance hit as the ide does transfers (eats up 100% of the processor).

(smile) I've often wondered if one of the promise cards and an ide
a/v stripped 'stack' would work on one of these machines.
     



