Richard Witte wrote:
> 
> I just acquired and AlphaStation and have a few questions. The machine came
> without the Update Firmware CD-ROM.
> Where can I get this CD-ROM?
> Can the AlphaStation 200 Series 4/233 use the Matrox Millenium II graphics
> board?
> And can this card be used with both the SRM and ARC console firmware?
> 
> Thanks in advance,
> 
> Richard

You can get the firmware off the web from DEC's ftp site. Using the
Millenium card will depend on driver availability. What operating system
are you using?

You need to be a bit careful with the Alphastation 200 series when it
comes to loading firmware. Some only have one ROM onboard so it's a case
of either SRM
or ARC. If your machine is one of these then you need to reload the
firmware
each time you want to change from SRM to ARC.

Joe




