  While noteworthy, it is not as impressive as if dell had announced
that they were shipping alpha systems that will run unix or NT.  The
netapp filer is simply a box that pumps correctly formatted data from
its pile of disk drives to client systems via some protocol.  Network
Appliance sold filers that used the 486 and pentium; now they sell
filers that use the alpha.  They run a totally custom hand crafted
"operating system" that is suited only for this single task.  They may
as well be using a bunch of DSPs or a PA-RISC cpu, or conductive fungus,
for all the client systems care.

  Announcing that Dell "Adopts Alpha" is like saying "Buick is selling
Ford cars!" when actually Buick is using a fuel injection control
computer designed by ford and made/sold by a third company.

  I think this announcement attacks microsoft more than intel, because
the filer boxes represent a very very high end NT server that will 
never be sold.
chris

