Paul,

I'm not sure which model of Celebris 560 motherboard you have.  Maybe
you have a later model than the ones I've seen, which support only the
Pentium 90 and Pentium 100.  Even tho the board has a Socket 5, it is
incapable of generating the 2x signals on the CPU CLKMUL pins, and
there is on jumper to change between 1.5x and 2x.

I'm trying to put together an unofficial ('cause I sure don't work for
Compaq) list of motherboard part numbers that fit inside the older
Celebris/Venturis chassis.  I got a couple of slightly less old
surplus Celebris and Venturis systems lately and they each have
motherboards that handle up to a P200... Ben Myers






