Philipp Buehler <pb@xlink108.xlink.net> writes:
> Oh, thx. Didn't got that information before.
> (What the hell is SDI? :) )

  Standard Disk Interconnect or somesuch.

> Btw, why is VMS (5.5-1) showing DUA0: in 'show device' as an RA81 - it
> is ESDI in fact !?

  Because you have an 3rd-party MSCP-emulating controller. They have to
report something for the disk type. Actually, only the RA part is fixed -
they can report any number for the 81. They normally pick the closest
matching DEC disk to the actual disk size, although some controllers al-
ways report RA81. Some controllers (the Webster ones come to mind) let
you set any digits you want. However, using a number that doesn't exist
as a DEC drive will likely confuse at least some software - for example,
an RA27.

