Stephen,

I have not yet had hands-on with a Starion 700i, but the BIOS in some
older Intel-made (and other-made) motherboards does have a 2.1GB limit
on EIDE hard disk size.  The circa 1995 Starion 700i BIOS is old
enough that it may have the 2.1GB limit, rather than 8.4GB.  The only
ways to find out are to try a larger hard drive and to determine the
Intel motherboard model from the BIOS signature, which may have been
covered up by DEC.  (Compaq, Dell, HP, IBM and others use Intel-made
boards, but often go to great pains to disguise the original equipment
manufacturer.)

As background, starting with older 486s, the BIOSes have progressively
had limits of 528MB, 2.1GB, and 8.4GB.  Some oddball BIOSes have other
quirks in handling hard disks... Ben Myers

