All original Starion systems shipped with a BIOS that only supported disks up to 2.1 GB.

The 700i is limited to 2.1GB. The later Starions (911, 915,917, 919, 921, 922, 930, 931,
933, 940, 950, 960) have a BIOS upgrade available that moves the limit to 7.9GB.

As Ben points out, the Starion tower systems were designed to the Western Digital LPx
form factor so that users could upgrade the motherboard/riser.

glen kelley
compaq

