James W. Caldwell wrote:
> 
> My 500au came with a 10baseT bnc adapter on the built in ethernet
> and now that I have 100baseT available the conversion kit is no
> longer available.  So DEC sold me a DE500-BA 100baseT PCI card
> (for a reasonable price) instead and I've just installed it and talked
> to it at the >>> prompt.
> 
> Now I can't figure out how to make 4.0D use it instead of tu0
> (the old card).  Do I need to edit rc.config and add tu1?
> Do I also need to remove tu0 since the machine only has
> one ethernet address?  Also, is there any other file(s) besides
> rc.config that needs changing.
> 
> Thanks,
> jim

This is a two step process. First off you have to rebuild the kernel so
it knows the new card is there. The easiest way is to add a line in the
config file  (/usr/sys/conf/machinename usually) eg

controller tu1 at pcix	slot  y

substituting your appropriate values for x & y.

One it shows up during the startup process you can configure it through
the network setup utility. Deconfigure the the original card at the same
time.

Don't forget to set the console variables so the DE500 actually uses
fast ethernet.

Enjoy.

Joe




