TO:  All Current User of RT-11 and TSX-PLUS

This post is divided into 5 sections.

1.  The Actual Announcement
     Patches are now available to be released to all commercial users of RT-11
     to enable Year 2000 operation of most (and probably all) of the most
     frequently used system and utility files for V5.4G of RT-11.   OTHER versions
     depending upon the demand.  At present, the monitor files (including RT11FB
     and RT11XM) are Year 2000 compliant.  All of the tape handlers are also
     available.  And finally, seven of the most important utilities are available including:
     DIR,  PIP,  LINK,  LIBR,  IND,  BUP and MACRO
     now have patches available so that they are Year 2000 compliant.  Note that
     depending upon demand, the other files such as QUEMAN,  SP(X).SYS and
     RTMON.REL  will also be made available.

2.  The Disclaimer
     See previous post on  Monday,  19-Oct-1998  07:25:23

3.  The Historical Background
     These patches were field tested for about a year and have been in production
     for an additional 9 months in a PDP-11 system which is in a Nuclear Generating
     Station.

     For complete details, see previous post on  Monday,  19-Oct-1998  07:25:23.

4.  Other Considerations and Contact Information
     The use of the Year 2000 patches will likely not resolve all of your Year 2000
     compliance problems.  In addition to the operating system, any lack of Year 2000
     compliance in the application programs must also be fixed.  For those using a
     custom generated monitor file, the fitting of the patches may not be trivial.
     Consequently, I suggest that if you wish to make any inquires, please provide
     the following information:

          Actual RT-11 and TSX-PLUS versions you are using
          A short, but complete, description of the hardware.
          A few sentences to describe the overall application.
          Your goals as to why you are considering the continued use of RT-11/TSX-PLUS.
          What kind of user you are: Commercial/Hobby

     While this initial inquiry is primarily for commercial users, hobby users are also
     encouraged to respond to provide as complete a picture as possible as to just
     how much interest there is in Year 2000 patches for all versions of RT-11.  It
     is possible that there is very substantial interest and a need for Year 2000
     patches for many versions of RT-11.

