supposed to run? Or did I somehow
>install the RAM incorrectly? What I have right now is 8 in
each of the first two slots
>and 4 in the next two.
>
Run SYSGEN and look at the PHYSICALPAGES parameter.  That's
the number of physical pages VMS will use, regardless of how
much ou have installed.  Chances are it's set to 32768
(16MB).  Try setting it to -1 to use all available memory.
I think AUTOGEN does this on some VMS vversions, for some
odd reason DEC assumes you will never upgrade memory.  Given
the historic pricing of DEC memory, this may be a valid
assumption.
>
