In article <78fvqd$me2$2@news3.microserve.net>, etienne_@microserve.net 
		(Stephen Eickhoff) writes:
> Yay!  Got my 4000/60 up and running.  However, I just installed two 4 MB
> modules in it to bring it up to 24 MB, but I can't get VMS to recognize it. 
> The boot check shows the 24, but "show mem" says 16.  Is there something I'm
> supposed to run?

        Yes.  On VAXen, you must  _always_  run  AUTOGEN and reboot when
    increasing  memory  in  order  for VMS to  "see"  the  total  memory
    present.  [Also, beware recommendations from those who don't know an
    Alpha from a VAX and then suggest running SYSGEN directly to set  an
    unphysical value for PHYSICALPAGES or "PHYSICALMEMORY"...]  Do check
    your  system's  MODPARAMS.DAT   and   _remove_  any  occurrances  of
    PHYSICALPAGES you might find there _before_ running AUTOGEN.
  
        -Ken
