Absolutely! Not too long ago I was researching third-party G3 cards for
Macintoshes, about as close to a commodity market as memory, and I
established a pretty clear 2.5 power relationship between price and
performance. That is, other factors (like cache size, vendor, etc.)
being equal, the price of a cpu card was proportional to its speed
raised to the 2.5 power. A spot check of Intel cpu upgrades showed the
same relationship. You will always find the best price/performance ratio
at the bottom of the performance curve because of the "gotta have it"
factor at the other end.



