I have a DEC Alphastation 255 running OSF3.2D. Recently it refused to
successfully boot. I tracked the problem down to a single command.
During the boot process the system issues "mount -u /" to remount the
root_device to / as read/write. This fails with the error message
"memory fault". I thought it might be the command but I can remount
other partitions from ro to rw using eg "mount -u /usr". Has anyone
encountered this problem before and found a solution?

Cheers

