In comp.sys.dec John Furcht <johnfurcht@worldnet.att.net> wrote:
> I have an MVII, that now requires me to enter the date and time on bootup.
> Is there a battery in these machines that hold the settings after power
> down?

  Yes.

> If so where is it located, where can I get one, and how do I install it?

  It is mounted to the inside back of the cabinet kit (the back panel piece
with the 7-segment LED display, switches, and console cable).

  It should have a part number on it (like xx-xxxxx-xx). If you call 800-
DIGITAL you should be able to order one from them. Or you can go to Radio
Shack and look at the cordless phone battery packs and find one with the
same cells. You'll need to transfer the connector from your pack to the
new one (and be sure to get the polarity right!).

  Note that if it's remembering the boot device, the problem may not be
with the battery - could be the clock, or (if you're running VMS) the
SYSGEN parameter that forces setting the time.

