We see it all the time.  It's not uncommon for our fortran codes to gain
a 2x performance boost when going from -O to -O5 optimization under the DEC
Fortran 90 compiler.  On certain codes 
"-speculate_all" will yield another
20% and on others it gives no improvement.  It seems a bit silly to spend
days or weeks coding up a problem and then use base optimization levels,
especially if this is a code that is to be run for hundreds of CPU hours.

