Greg Pfister <pfister@usNOSPAM.ibm.com> writes:


> What about non-NUMA directory-based cache-coherence systems? Done with a
> crossbar, it can be UMA. That snooping has problems doesn't necessarily
> mean that UMA has problems.

Correct but the problem is that to do a UMA directory-based CC system,
you are most likely going to have to use a full cross bar.  

The point of the original comment that I made was, once you are going
to some sort of cross bar, why not take full advantage of all that it
gives you.  In a system like the UE10k, you end up adding a lot of
latency because of the complex multi-stage switch needed to create a
full crossbar.  

What I would rather see is people taking advantage of the cross bars
better by going to non-uniform access.  It can be easily
conceptualized as have worst case latency no worse than the fully
connected crossbar and average latencies that are much better.



Aaron Spink
