John Furcht <johnfurcht@worldnet.att.net> wrote:
>I have an MVII, that now requires me to enter the date and time on bootup.
>Is there a battery in these machines that hold the settings after power
>down?
>If so where is it located, where can I get one, and how do I install it?
>
>Thanks, John

Yes, there is a battery backup for the MVII. Depending on your box type
(BA23, or BA123) it should be near the dials that allow you to set your
system to boot automatically or stop at the >>> prompt. On the inside of 
that pannel there is a white plastic shrink wrapped package. What is under
that is two or three (I've forgotten the exact number) of AA or AAA 
batteries connected in series (or was that parallel, it has been a while).

You can cut away the white plastic and see the type of batteries that are
there and how they are wired. Then just replace the batteries, wiring them
in the same manner as the original ones.

What the batteries do is keep enough power to the CPU to maintaine the
date and time.


