>

I think on the power supply itself is a small label with the ratings of the
outputs. At 12 volts you may only go up to about 0.3 Amps if I recall correctly.

And since the fan uses up 0.12 already there's not much left...

My UDB runs with an internal IBM 2.1 Gb SCSI which uses (according to the
label) 0.2 Amps at 12 Volt. The 5 volt supply can handle some more but
I would not want to draw more than 0.5 either... The 4 pin connector on the
edge of the PCI bus/SCSI board has 5 and 12 volt outputs.

(I also have a PCI VGA card in there, and I replaced the temperature
controlled fan by a fixed speed one, gives some more noise but runs the
system a lot cooler...)


