In comp.sys.dec John Furcht <johnfurcht@worldnet.att.net> wrote:
> I have an MVII, that now requires me to enter the date and time on bootup.
> Is there a battery in these machines that hold the settings after power
> down?

The battery used in a lot of DEC equipment is a Panasonic battery pack.

The DEC part number is 12-19254-00.
It also has the following Panasonic Nos: NRAAA 1/A 47/F

It can be found in a uVax II, uVax 2000, DECstation 2100 & 3100. 
In each case the battery pack is just mounted in a different plastic holder
which has its own part number.  I suspect that it also the same one used in 
the 5000, 5400, and 5500.

Mike




