Nope, that doesn't always work.  If your SYSGEN parameter is
set lower than actual physical memory, you won't get the
true installed RAM size.  Use the SHOW MEM in the boot ROM
instead, or make sure the SYSGEN parameter (PHYSICALPAGES)
is set to -1 so it autoconfigures memory size.
           Jack Peacock




