>Carl Perkins wrote:
>> 
>> I have a DEC 3000 model 600. It has an "alternate console" serial port.
>> This port is evidently fixed to exactly 9600bps (and other specifics).
>> Is there any way to convince the hardware to allow different settings?
>
>Not according to the hardware guide I'm looking at. Page 12-2 says they
>are fixed settings.

If this is somehow connected to the SROM debug port, then no, I don't think
it can be changed, period.

[...]
>> As far as I can tell nobody ever made a serial port card for the
>> Turbochannel bus. Is this correct?

I don't believe so -- at one point we looked at using a DECstation 5000/25
with a TC serial card (CD1400-based, as I recall) as a UUCP machine, so
I'm pretty sure such cards existed.  Device drivers for some modern version
of OSF/1 might be hard to come by, but you could concievably run NetBSD and
port the driver for the very, very similar Sbus cards -- or pay someone
to do so.  (I can probably find you someone to do this if you have the
hardware available).

Magma made them for SPARCstations with Sbus -- I can't remember if they're
where we looked when we needed one for TurboChannel, but it wouldn't be a
bad bet.  We also looked at SCSI serial port expansion boxes, which may
still be available and *may* have OSF/1 device drivers.

