Garfield Cat <garfieldcat@writeme.com> writes...
}  I encountered a insufficient virtual memory error on sorting a larger
}file. Is there any way to increase virtual memory?

Assuming VMS...

Have the system manager increase your pagefile quota (PGFLQUO) and/or
your working set size (probably the extent, i.e. WSEXTENT) process
quotas for you via the authorize utility. If they are already at the
maximums allowed by the relevant system parameters, then those parameters
would have to be increased (VIRTUALPAGECNT and WSMAX could be relevant -
both require a reboot for changes to take effect (at least they do under
VMS version 6.1 - newer versions may allow dynamic alteration)). It could
also require increasing the size of the system's pagefile(s).

--- Carl



