On Fri, 15 Jan 1999, John Mullett wrote:

> It is true that the firware BIOS needs to be either ARC or AlphaBIOS to
> install NT and even Linux for that matter, and some system only have the
> SRM firmware which is used with Unix and VMS.  This can be changed quite

 Linux works very well with SRM.  In fact, for some systems it's the only
configuration supported.  Linux can be booted from SRM directly -- for
ARC, Linux needs an intermediate loader called MILO, which loads
appropriate PALcode and performs necessary hardware initializaton.  And
yes, Linux supports disklabels.

