From the number that your showing it seems that the page allocation is
fully local or >95% local, resulting in roughly the same performance
and scaling you would get in you put 16 2 processors O2k or O200 on
ethernet and ran specrate in parallel.  

So, I was wondering if I am correct in the page allocation strategy
and what the numbers look like if you do a random or farthest neighbor
page allocation?  

The reason I ask this is because of both the inherent advantages and
disadvantages of a NUMA style system design.  Since programs
themselves can behave differently as far as performance depending on
where the actual memory is allocated, it would be interesting to see
how on a given implementation, things change going from optimal to
sub-optimal to worst case.

You probably can't give specific numbers, but even a general
qualitative analysis would be interesting.


Aaron Spink
