 You don't say what operating system you are running (it does make a
difference :-) )

For DIGITAL UNIX

/sbin/swapon /dev/rz1b

will add partition rz1b as a swap area. Make sure the partition exists
and doesn't overlap other partitions on the disk. See "man swapon" for
full details. Normally the swap devices are defined in /etc/fstab, so
they are set up at boot time.

For OpenVMS:

RUN SYS$SYSTEM:SYSGEN
SYSGEN> CREATE DISK:[DIR]SWAPFILE.SYS/SIZE=100000/CONTIG
SYSGEN> INSTALL DISK:[DIR]SWAPFILE.SYS/SWAPFILE

will create and make active a swapfile (/PAGE gives a pagefile).
Normally the INSTALL command is placed in
SYS$MANAGER:SYPAGSWPFILES.COM, so it is invoked early in the
boot sequence.

Regards,
John Hill

