Terence Murphy wrote:

> I was wondering about getting Windows NT running on an Alpha system.

Your NT 4.0 CD media works on multiple platforms including Alpha, Intel,
and MIPS and will install on these platforms quite easily. Legally you
will have to have a valid license for each workstation you plan to
install NT on.

It is true that the firware BIOS needs to be either ARC or AlphaBIOS to
install NT and even Linux for that matter, and some system only have the
SRM firmware which is used with Unix and VMS.  This can be changed quite
easily even if your system only allows one BIOS to be installed in the
ROM.

I've run NT 4.0 on systems as slow as a Multia 21066 AXP 166 MHz (read
low cache cheap processor) system and 64 MB of ram, and it is fully
capable of general desktop performance and moderately impressive on some
floating point intensive ray tracing applications.

You might try pointing your browser to www.alphant.com for more
information on running NT on DEC Alpha systems. Good luck!



