Andrew Hargreave wrote:

> Let me start by saying I know next to nothing about configuring a DEC
> Alpha..so be gentle <g>
>
> We had purchased this box from a client a couple years ago, it had OpenVMS
> installed on it for a database.  The client/project is long gone and the box
> was sitting in the closet collecting dust.  I purchased Red Hat Linux/Alpha
> v5.2
>
> and am trying to get it up and running.  I was able to get the install to
> run and it reformatted the 2 partitions, etc..but upon reboot, says that "
>
> block 0 of dka300.3.0.6.0 is not a valid boot block..bootstrap failure"
>

Seems like Milo isn't installed properly..
For general info on running linux on alpha's have a peek at

www.alphalinux.org

>
> I have no idea how to partition the drives, etc...I had hoped that the
> install routine had done it, but apparently not correctly.  Here are some
> machine specs if it will help you help me <g>
>

Normally you partition the drive using fdisk (or disk-druid)
for booting these systems you need a small ms-dos partition with milo on it.
(my alpha UDB/Multia has 3 partitions: a small (2 Mb) MS-DOS (12 bit FAT),
a reasonable amount of swapspace (twice memory size, although with 128 Mb
this might be overkill) and a native linux partition.

>

Gert

