There is also a proxy file called NETPROXY.DAT that you might want to copy
if you have set up any proxies in authorize (with the add/proxy command).  

You will get all your users back inf you preserve those three files.  Now
thats just the accounts, not the directory's of course.  If you have the
their directories on the system disk (I have seen systems like that!) then
you will have to back those to another disk.

You should preserve other site specific stuff that you may have edited. 
You may want to survery the files that have been edited on the disk in the
last year with a dir/since.  Especially save the systartup_vms.com and
sylogin.com, but don't copy them back, merge your site specific stuff into
the new one created from the 7.1 install.  You really have to know your
system directories, and remember what you have added to files like
systartup_vms.com in order to do this effectively.

Scott

