Aaron Spink wrote:

> IIRC, the POWER3 systems actually have a higher bandwidth connection
> to the chipset than EV6.  Something like 200mhz by 128 bits comes to
> mind.

  The Power3 has a 256 by 200 MHz L2 cache bus and a 128 bit by 100 MHz
  system bus.  The data cache line size is 128 bytes.  The huge line
  size helps STREAM and SPECfp95 scores at the cost of poorer SPECint95
  performance (but who would buy a Power3 system to run integer code?).

  BTW, the Power3 package has 1088 pins vs the 588 for the 21264.

> 
