I remember "band-too-complex" quite well. The original LN03 did not have 
enough memory to print an arbitrary page. If you changed from black to white 
(or vice versa) too often on a line (or was it per page?) then the printer ran 
out of memory to process the line (or page) and gave you" band too complex".

The fix was to upgrade to the LN03+ which could cope quite nicely.

I remember hitting this occasionally when trying to print particularly 
complicated pages produced using TeX. If you are using Ghostscript to turn 
postscript into something else then this may be your problem.

If you already have an LN03R (the LN03 ScriptWriter) then this is supposed to 
have fixed the badn-too-complex problem (but it also understands postscript 
directly so you wouldn't need GhostScript so I presume that you have an 
ordinary LN03).

>Is there a document available that explains the control codes and
>escape sequences? This would allow me to build a test script and
>validate the ghostscript output. The test sheet says Rev Level
>DEC004.4, Cartridge 1 and 2 are both RAM, and there is 283Kb available
>for fonts.

There were programmer's manuals for both the LN03 and LN03R IIRC but I don't 
have them myself and I don't know if they are still available.

Antonio

