> Don't believe Gartner.  They've been saying VMS is dead longer
> than there have been pizza parties at the White House.


Back in the early 1980's I had consultants telling potential customers to go
with Prime and Wang based solutions instead of the PDP-11 based solution we
were offering at that time.  The consultant's POV was that the PDP-11
wouldn't supported by Digital for more than a few years and the Prime and
Wang 32-bit platforms would be supported into the next century.  No one had
a VAX based product at that time in this market.  Well we all know what
happened to Wang and Prime.  I actually have a customer still running on a
PDP-11 platform with no support problems...

IMHO the PDP-11, unlike the DECsystem10 and 20, went through a very nice end
of life program which the OVMS community should closely consider.  The basic
decision that was made was to extend what the PDP-11 did well and not try to
break new ground trying to turn into VAX2.  It does raise concern when OVMS
fans seem to promote the concept that OVMS should break new ground and chase
the market rather than focus on rounding out its functionality where OVMS's
strengths exists.   Like it or not the opportunity for OVMS becoming a
volume operating has pasted.

Re: The Alpha - the reality is that decision will be driven by market forces
and not by technological evaluation.  Despite the legitimate scorn folks
have for MS technology there is a strong force in the market to achieve a
universal platform.  Fortunately the Alpha is a safe bet for W2K development
because if Intel really does deliver, making the Alpha questionable, at
worst one is looking at a recompile.  But market forces will still make this
a game where Alpha's fate is primarily a function of Intel's ability to
execute i.e. it is their game to loose.  While the Alpha may have strengths
its strengths would have to be significantly better than Intel's chips to
justify maintaining two binary code bases.

For now if one is a fan of OVMS or DUNIX one should look favorably upon as
many W2K Alpha based systems as possible being sold.  Volume in the end will
protect the platform for OVMS and DUNIX...







