I had this problem when I joined my current project. I will not bore you with
backup
scare stories, but several sites were, depending on the time of the month,
database
maintenenance schedule etc, running onto a second tape for the daily backup.
Some
sites, the users were locked out while the second tape ran, meaning they
couldn't
start work untill that tape had been loaded, written, verified etc. At least
they got
a good backup, they just started work later. Other sites did not have user
lockout, their
backups were barely useful (I did some restores from the old scripts but luckily
after
I had been in and added a few essential backup tweaks).

My solution was to buy larger capacity tape drives, and fair-do's, the
management
went for it. My biggest systems run at about 10 gig so a single drive was
adequate,
otherwise I'd have gone for an autoloaded I guess.

That is the only way you will get a decent full backup every night anyway.


