In article <36932930.54D8849A@comarch.pl>, Pawel Wnek <wnek@comarch.pl> writes:
|> Hi everybody!
|> 
|> I have the following question: how to increase number of ptys on Digital
|> Unix 3.2G. The default value is 32 and it is not enough for me.
|> 
|> Greetz
|> Pawel
|> 

As root,

# cd /dev
# ./MAKEDEV PTY_2		# will add ptys 32 to 45
# ./MAKEDEV PTY_3		# will add ptys 46 to 56
# ./MAKEDEV PTY_4		# will add ptys 57 to 64
# ./MAKEDEV PTY_5		# will add ptys 65 to 72
# ./MAKEDEV PTY_6		# will add ptys 73 to 80
# ./MAKEDEV PTY_7		# will add ptys 81 to 88
# ./MAKEDEV PTY_8		# will add ptys 89 to 96
# ./MAKEDEV PTY_9		# will add ptys 97 to 101
#

Or, in one fell swoop:

# cd /dev
# ./MAKEDEV PTY_2 PTY_3 PTY_4 PTY_5 PTY_6 PTY_7 PTY_8 PTY_9

You might want to bump up the value of 'maxusers' in
/sys/conf/YOUR_MACHINE_NAME and rebuild the kernel.
The default value is 32.

Best regards,
=Aaron
