Yes, the drive itself would have to make stats available on how much
compression had been achieved, and the /STAT qualifier would need to
pass that on. It would be a very useful addition. It would be nice if
there were an option to put the stats into DCL symbols etc, so that
automated backups could easily take action based on the values (eg tape
nearly full).



