I need 3 because the Switches/Hubs on the 3 interfaces are not connected
together elsewhere - if data goes into one switch then it cannot get to the
other two by any other route. My statement was unclear, but to try another
summary :-

The UCX SHOW ROUTE command shows the networks and gateways (similar to the
following) :-

                         DYNAMIC database
Type  Destination                         Gateway
AH    127.0.0.1                            127.0.0.1
AN    a.b.0.0                                a.b.0.1

But if I add 2 more interfaces then its likely to add 2 more lines...

AN    a.b.0.0                                a.b.0.2
AN    a.b.0.0                                a.b.0.3

And when a packet arrives on one interface (likely to work) - say the 3rd
interface the reply will be routed back using the routing table via the
first interface since IP only knows that a packet arrived - I doubt it knows
which interface it came in on, just which interface (using the routing
table) to send it to to get it back there. I'm going to try this tonight
since the DE500-BA's I ordered have just arrived.

