Jerry Leslie wrote:
> 
> One of our sites has had problems with its computer room A/C,
> resulting in the computer rooms operating without A/C for some
> period of time.
> 
> What VAXes & ALPHAs, if any, have high temperature shutdown devices ?
> 
> I remember that the VAX 82xx-83xx and probably some others have
> a sensor that will power the system down if the air flow through
> the system is blocked, but what about a VAX 4000/200 or
> a VAXStation 4000/90 ?

I can't talk about those models.  The VAX-11/750 did have high
temperature shutdown.  In a previous existence we had an A/C failure
that baked the system up to that point.  It was about six months
afterwards before we had a reliable system again:  the initial damage
seemed to be limited to one power supply and two power supply fans,
but things just kept breaking and needing Field Servants' attention
every few weeks.  The conclusion I drew was that the temperature
at which it stopped working was probably already too high, or the
shutdown did not reduce power consumption enough to keep the baking
at a mild enough temperature. 

