The problems start when putting a std::list in a std::hash_map
and compiling -O.

I checked the egcs web-page, and it's not a known-bug.
Egcs recommends sending a .ii file as bug report, but as that
one is over 300Kb, I thought it would not be the right thing to
do. (It grows so large because of all the STL).

Has anyone else experienced problems with STL and egcs?

Thanks,
         Bram

For the interested, this is the src that crashes:

/*
 * This is the minimalized code to demonstrate an
 * eledged bug in egcc when putting STL-lists in an STL-hash_map
 *
