Robert Miller <rgmiller@home.com> writes:
>     I need to purchase a cdrom for my AS200. I read that it needs  to read
> 512KB blocks. Is that correct, 

  512-byte sectors. Yes. The standard CD-ROM sector size is 2048 bytes, but
DEC (and Sun, and some others) want to be different. Note that not only must
the drive support 512-byte sectors, but it needs to be configured that way.
Many drives support the 512-byte sectors, but only via a SCSI Mode Select
command, not by a permanent config change.

> The cdrom I'm looking to get is a NEC scsi
> 6Xi from pricewatch.com. It's about 50 bucks
> Any suggestions or help is greatly appreciated

  I have no experience with that drive on the AS200. However, I should men-
tion that many older drives, even ones that support 512-byte sectors, have
problems on this system. For example, DEC's own RRD42 (an OEM'd Sony CDU-
541) isn't supported for this reason.

  I bought a new Plextor UltraPlex 32TSi. They guarantee compatibility with
the Alpha under both NT and VMS. The list price is $179. If that's within
your budget and you'll be doing a lot of installs from CD (and so a faster
drive will help), I'd suggest it.

