That doesn't look right according to the diagram I have
for the TK50 (M7546).   According to it, with the handle end
up and the card edge connector down, it should look like:

A12  o=o         +--- Hardware Revision Level (Binary)
A11  o=o         |    (Switch 0 is low-order bit)
A10  o o         V    (1 = Rev A, 2 = Rev B, 3 = Rev C, etc.)
A 9  o o       +---+
A 8  o=o      0|*  |       +--- Unit Number (Binary)
A 7  o o      1|  *|       |    (Switch 0 is low-order bit)
A 6  o=o      2|  *|       V
A 5  o o      3|*  |     +---+
A 4  o o      4|*  |    0|*  |
A 3  o o      5|*  |    1|*  |
A 2  o o      6|*  |    2|*  |
              7|*  |    3|*  |
               +---+    4|*  |
                        5|*  |
                        6|*  |
                        7|*  |
                         +---+

Also, the default CSR for a TK50 is 17774500, not 17772150.
The address jumpers for 17774500 are A12, A11, A8, and A6.
The default interrupt vector for a TK50 is 260, but it is
set via software (driver) control.

